Short:        Mail for AmigaOS 3: IMAP, TLS, OAuth
Uploader:     (We fill this in at upload time)
Author:       Dalsin Limited
Type:         comm/mail
Version:      0.3.1
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.0+, a TCP/IP stack, AmiSSL 5
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0
Distribution: Aminet

OpenMail is a free mail client for AmigaOS 3.x, written from the
standards (RFC 3501, 5321, 5322, MIME) with a GadTools interface.

What it does today
------------------
- Reads mail over IMAP, with TLS or STARTTLS and the certificate checked
  (AmiSSL 5).
- Signs in with a password or an OAuth token (XOAUTH2).
- Shows folders, the newest messages (unread and flagged marked), and
  each message as text: multipart mail, quoted-printable and base64,
  common character sets, HTML turned into readable text with its links
  numbered. Nothing is fetched to show a message, so there are no
  tracking pixels.
- "View in browser" opens a message's HTML in your web browser, and
  "Links..." opens any of its links: through ENV:OpenMail/Browser (a
  command with %s), AmigaChrome's browser, or OpenURL.
- Talks to the servers from a process of its own, so the window never
  freezes while mail comes in.

Writing, replying and an account window come in the next version.

Providers and sign-in methods are plugins
-----------------------------------------
A mail service is a small text file in Providers/ (Gmail, Outlook.com,
Yahoo, iCloud and Fastmail are included); anyone can add one. Sign-in
methods are Amiga libraries behind one interface, so new ones can be
added without changing OpenMail.

Installing
----------
Copy the OpenMail drawer anywhere. Until the account window arrives,
the account is a text file, ENV:OpenMail/Account (see README.md).

